-- Registry blocker B24 (docs/implementation/product-v1-closure-20260926/finalization-20260927/ROUND_74_P6_PHYSICAL_HONOR_CANDIDATE.md): PostgREST 14 re-executes,
-- without end and after the client has gone, any request whose function raises SQLSTATE 40001 (proof run 36745783626; Supabase documents the same defect: PostgREST 14
-- affected, 16 fixed, use a custom or P0001 code instead). Every one of the 89 sites below is a DETERMINISTIC business conflict (a stale revision, token, digest or
-- idempotency mismatch, classified one by one in docs/.../b24/B24_SITE_CLASSIFICATION.md): a retry of the same call can never succeed, so the retry is pure harm.
-- None is an engine-raised serialization failure (those come from Postgres itself, are not in any function body, and are not touched).
--
-- What this changes: in 54 functions the code of each such raise becomes PT409 (PostgREST answers HTTP 409 at once, with the same message), and nothing else:
-- same message, same arguments, same security, same grants, same comment. None of these functions is among the 76 that `private.closure_source_digest_v5()` hashes, so the certified digest must NOT move:
-- the candidate asserts that before and after, and refuses to run twice. Part 2 covers the 14 certified functions and re-binds the certificate.
