-- Guards: every target exists exactly once, carries exactly the pinned number of quoted '40001' and no 'PT409' yet; in strict mode (the default) its body md5 equals the pre-image
-- read from canonical DEV on 2026-09-30; afterwards its body with PT409 turned back into 40001 is byte-for-byte the old body, it has no 40001 left, its owner/ACL/security/config/comment
-- tuple is unchanged, and the only functions still raising 40001 are the certified ones of part 2. A disposable proof database that does not carry the DEV pre-image runs it with
